WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.467
Rules connect when the complete result of one supplies the complete sufficient condition of another.

2
00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:10.244
Following those connections establishes a new conditional.

3
00:00:10.544 --> 00:00:12.379
Every scanned chart is indexed.

4
00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.407
Every indexed chart is stored.

5
00:00:14.707 --> 00:00:16.157
Imagine a scanned chart.

6
00:00:16.457 --> 00:00:18.207
The first rule gives indexing.

7
00:00:18.507 --> 00:00:21.387
That satisfies the second rule and gives storage.

8
00:00:21.687 --> 00:00:23.585
So every scanned chart is stored.

9
00:00:23.885 --> 00:00:26.189
No scanned chart was asserted to exist.

10
00:00:26.489 --> 00:00:31.503
If Chart F is later said to be scanned, the chain then establishes storage for F.

11
00:00:31.803 --> 00:00:35.728
A chain makes a passage’s separate guarantees available together.

12
00:00:36.028 --> 00:00:42.663
An answer may use the whole chain or a shorter segment, so do not memorize only the first-to-last result.

13
00:00:42.963 --> 00:00:46.120
Write the first result beside the next sufficient condition.

14
00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:48.020
Read both labels in full.

15
00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.541
If one needs something more, the connection is incomplete.

16
00:00:51.841 --> 00:00:54.188
Add a clear connection as you encounter it.

17
00:00:54.488 --> 00:00:58.669
If the matching takes effort, write the rules separately first, then align them.

18
00:00:58.969 --> 00:01:04.345
Keep the page readable rather than duplicating every contrapositive without a purpose.
